From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@loudthinking.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:38:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Drop cluster_cl5 idle state from
 CPU clusters

The cluster_cl5 idle state triggers random hard freezes and spontaneous
restarts on Glymur (Snapdragon X2) laptops such as the ASUS Zenbook A16
(UX3607OA), matching the hamoa cluster_cl5 issue mitigated in
2151-arm64-dts-qcom-hamoa-Drop-cluster_cl5-idle-state-fro.patch.

Drop domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5> from cluster0_pd, cluster1_pd
and cluster2_pd while keeping the per-CPU cpu_c4 retention state intact.

Closes: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues/19916
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
index 212f9fbad..68bae8ba4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
@@ -568,19 +568,16 @@
 		cluster0_pd: power-domain-cpu-cluster0 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
-			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5>;
 		};
 
 		cluster1_pd: power-domain-cpu-cluster1 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
-			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5>;
 		};
 
 		cluster2_pd: power-domain-cpu-cluster2 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
-			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_cl5>;
 		};
 
 		system_pd: power-domain-system {
